+    <section id="roasters-journal" class="journal-section">
+      <div class="journal-header">
+        <h2>Roaster's Journal: Our Bean Sourcing Process</h2>
+        <button id="summarize-btn" class="btn" type="button">Summarize</button>
+      </div>
+      <article id="journal-text" class="journal-content">
+        <p>Every exceptional cup of coffee begins long before the beans ever reach our roastery. For the past decade, our sourcing team has traveled to high-altitude micro-lots across Ethiopia, Colombia, and Guatemala to build direct-trade partnerships with smallholder farmers. By bypassing traditional commodity supply chains, we ensure that our partner growers receive at least 40% above Fair Trade baseline prices, empowering them to reinvest in sustainable farming practices and local community infrastructure.</p>
+        <p>At altitudes between 1,600 and 2,200 meters above sea level, cooler mountain nights slow down the maturation of the coffee cherry. This extended growth cycle allows complex sugars and vibrant organic acids to develop within the seed, yielding the distinct floral, citrus, and stone-fruit notes that define our seasonal offerings. During harvest season, pickers selectively hand-harvest only the ripest crimson cherries, leaving unripe fruit on the branch for subsequent passes.</p>
+        <p>Once harvested, the cherries undergo meticulous processing at local washing stations. Depending on regional climate and flavor goals, lots are either washed in fresh mountain spring water and sun-dried on raised African beds or naturally fermented in their fruit pulp to enhance body and sweetness. Before any lot is approved for shipment, our certified Q-Graders conduct rigorous blind cuppings alongside the producers, scoring each batch on aroma, acidity, body, and clean finish.</p>
+        <p>Finally, the green coffee beans are sealed in hermetic GrainPro bags to lock in moisture content and protect against humidity during ocean transit. Upon arrival at our local roastery, we roast in small batches using custom temperature profiles tailored to each farm's terroir, bringing the full story of the harvest directly to your morning cup.</p>
+      </article>
+      <div id="journal-summary" class="journal-summary" aria-live="polite">
+        <h3>Key Takeaways</h3>
+        <div id="summary-output"></div>
+      </div>
+    </section>
